            <ArticleTitle>The effects of passive smoking on adult and child health.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>217-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Forty-two per cent of UK children live in a household where someone smokes. This paper, the third in a series on smoking cessation, presents a brief review of the evidence concerning the impact of passive smoking on adult and child health. It outlines some harm-reduction approaches aimed at reducing the impact of passive smoking at home, at work and in public.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
